T*
() Tj
T*
T*
(PURPOSE) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(This report documents the accessibility audit of the Memory Match game, explains why) Tj
T*
(the initial results were lower, and records improvements made after reviewing Lighthouse) Tj
T*
(findings. Each topic is covered once to avoid duplicated report sections.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
T*
(1. INITIAL AUDIT RESULTS) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Performance: 88/100 \(a later screenshot also showed 77\). Loading and rendering work) Tj
T*
(remained; scores can vary with device, network, cache, and test conditions.) Tj
T*
(Accessibility: 96/100. Some automated accessibility checks still needed attention.) Tj
T*
(Best Practices: 77/100. Lighthouse reported warnings; inspect diagnostics before assigning) Tj
T*
(a cause.) Tj
T*
(SEO: 90/100. The page was missing basic search metadata, including a meta description.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
T*
(2. WHY THE SCORES WERE LOW) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Performance: results indicated time spent rendering main content, possible render-blocking) Tj
T*
(CSS, and long main-thread tasks. These can delay Largest Contentful Paint \(LCP\). Scores) Tj
T*
(may differ between runs.) Tj
T*
(Accessibility: a score of 96 means at least one automated check was not passing. Manual) Tj
T*
(checks include keyboard focus, logical tab order, visible focus, and focus handling for) Tj
T*
(new content. These must be tested by a person.) Tj
T*
(Best Practices: the score of 77 showed warnings. The score alone does not identify the) Tj
T*
(cause, so review diagnostics rather than guessing.) Tj
T*
(SEO: the score of 90 was associated with missing page metadata, including a description.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
T*
(3. IMPROVEMENTS MADE) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Added a skip link as the first useful keyboard navigation option so keyboard users can) Tj
T*
(jump directly to the main content.) Tj
T*
(Added a main-content target using <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1"> so the skip) Tj
T*
(link can move focus to the main area.) Tj
T*
(Week 9 - Accessibility Audit | Page 1) Tj
T*
